IMPORT prelude

-- Republic Polytechnic Act 2002 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a student, a fee-payer, a donor or a lender: late-payment
-- charges and the validation of past ones (ss 5(2)(c), 5A), who may receive a diploma (s 12; Constitution s 1), who may end a
-- student's studies (Constitution ss 6(3)(c), 11(j)), when Board and Senate regulations take effect (Constitution ss 6(4), 12(2)),
-- the Students' Union and the Societies Act (s 16; Constitution s 19), execution under the common seal (s 4), borrowing (s 15),
-- the Board's size, terms, vacancies and voting (Constitution ss 2(5), 3(4), 5, 7, 8, 9), the Senate's quorum and meetings
-- (Constitution s 10), the financial year (Constitution s 14) and donations for a specific purpose (Constitution ss 17, 18).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/RPA2002.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 4 of 2008 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008), annotated "wef 01/04/2024" and
-- listed in the legislative history with commencement 1 April 2024. Section numbers follow the BODY: the arrangement of sections
-- at the top of the .txt deposit is out of step by one (it lists "2. Short title", while the body has "1. ... Short title").
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0201 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a student, fee-payer, donor, lender or counterparty meets, and the governance
-- rules that decide whether a decision affecting them was validly made. Not encoded: the Polytechnic's objects and general powers
-- beyond s 5(2)(c) (s 5), the Board and Senate as institutions (ss 6-9) beyond s 6(4)'s validity rule, the Minister's power to
-- amend the Constitution (s 10(2)), examinations (s 11; Constitution s 13), grants (s 13), shares issued to the
-- Minister for Finance (s 14), the officers' duties (Constitution ss 2-4) beyond voting, the Board's and Senate's lists of powers
-- (Constitution ss 6(1)-(3), 11) beyond ending studies, and estimates (Constitution ss 15, 16). The regulations made under the
-- Constitution (admission, fees, discipline) were not retrieved; s 10(3) says they "are not subsidiary legislation".
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Republic Polytechnic Act 2002`

§§ `5(2)(c) and 5A -- late-payment charges`

-- s 5(2)(c): the Polytechnic may "fix, demand and receive fees and other charges, including charges for the late payment of any such
-- fee or charge" [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024].
-- s 5A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or purportedly
-- as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or charge referred to in section 5(2)(c) shall be deemed to be and always to have been
-- validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or maintained in any court of law on account of or in
-- respect of any such collection."
-- The legislative history gives that Act's commencement as 1 April 2024. Dates are written as yyyymmdd numbers.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the commencement of Act 4 of 2008` MEANS 20240401

GIVEN `collected on` IS A NUMBER, `collected as a late-payment charge on a Polytechnic fee or charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5A deems the collection valid and bars proceedings` IF
        `collected as a late-payment charge on a Polytechnic fee or charge`
    AND `collected on` LESS THAN `the commencement of Act 4 of 2008`

§§ `12 and Constitution s 1 -- who may receive a diploma`

-- Constitution s 1(1): "registered student" means "a student who is registered for a course or subject at the Polytechnic, leading
-- to the award of a diploma, certificate or other academic distinction of the Polytechnic".
-- s 12: the Polytechnic may (a) award diplomas, certificates and other distinctions "specified in regulations made under the
-- Constitution"; and (b) "provide access to such educational activities and programmes for persons who are not registered students
-- as the Polytechnic may determine, and to award diplomas, certificates and other academic distinctions to those persons".
-- Constitution s 11(g): the Senate decides "in accordance with this Constitution and the regulations persons who are qualified".
-- That the Senate's decision governs the s 12(b) awards too is an INFERENCE: s 11(g) is not limited to registered students.
DECLARE Learner IS ONE OF
    `a student registered for a diploma course`
    `a student registered for a subject leading to a certificate`
    `a participant in a programme the Polytechnic opened to non-registered persons`
    `a member of the public at an open lecture the Polytechnic did not designate`

GIVEN `the learner` IS A Learner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the learner is a registered student` IF
    CONSIDER `the learner`
    WHEN `a student registered for a diploma course` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a student registered for a subject leading to a certificate` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the learner` IS A Learner, `the Senate decided the learner is qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Polytechnic may award the learner a diploma or certificate` IF
        (   `the learner is a registered student` `the learner`
         OR CONSIDER `the learner`
            WHEN `a participant in a programme the Polytechnic opened to non-registered persons` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `the Senate decided the learner is qualified`

§§ `Constitution ss 6(3)(c), 11(j) -- who may end a student's studies`

-- Constitution s 6(3): "The Board may by regulations provide for ... (c) the welfare, discipline, suspension and expulsion of students".
-- s 11: the Senate has power "(j) to require any student on academic grounds to terminate his or her studies at the Polytechnic".
-- s 2(3)(c): the Principal is responsible to the Board for "the welfare and discipline of the staff and students".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `academic grounds`
    `discipline`
    `non-payment of fees`

DECLARE Decider IS ONE OF
    `the Senate`
    `the Board, by regulations`
    `not settled by the Act`

-- Non-payment of fees: s 6(3)(f) lets the Board regulate "fees and other charges", but neither the Act nor the Constitution says
-- that a student may be removed for not paying. Returning `not settled by the Act` is the encoding's reading.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A Decider
`who may end the studies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `academic grounds` THEN `the Senate`
    WHEN `discipline` THEN `the Board, by regulations`
    OTHERWISE `not settled by the Act`

§§ `Constitution ss 6(4), 12(2) -- when regulations take effect`

-- s 6(4) (Board regulations): "come into operation on the day on which they are made unless otherwise provided by the Board".
-- s 12(2) (Senate regulations, which cover admission, award conditions, courses, examinations and scholarships): "must be reported to
-- the Board and come into operation not earlier than one semester after the day on which they are made, unless otherwise approved by
-- the Board".
-- s 10(3) of the Act: "Regulations made under the Constitution are not subsidiary legislation."
DECLARE Maker IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `the Senate`

GIVEN `the maker` IS A Maker, `the Board approved earlier operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum wait in semesters` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the maker`
    WHEN `the Board` THEN 0
    WHEN `the Senate` THEN IF `the Board approved earlier operation` THEN 0 ELSE 1

GIVEN `the maker` IS A Maker, `the Board approved earlier operation` IS A BOOLEAN, `semesters since made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulation may already be in operation` IF
    `semesters since made` AT LEAST `the minimum wait in semesters` `the maker` `the Board approved earlier operation`

§§ `16 and Constitution s 19 -- the Students' Union`

-- Constitution s 19(1): the Republic Polytechnic Students' Union "is constituted by regulations made by the Board". (3): "The
-- Polytechnic may impose and collect from the students or any class of students such fees as it may determine for the benefit of"
-- the Union and its constituent bodies; (4): those fees "may be applied in any manner that the Polytechnic thinks fit for the
-- purposes of" the Union and its constituent bodies.
-- s 16(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act apply to" the Union and its
-- constituent bodies constituted by regulations under the Constitution; (2): the Minister charged with societies "may, by order in
-- the Gazette, exempt" them "from all or any of the provisions" of that Act, subject to conditions.
GIVEN `for the purposes of the Union or its constituent bodies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Union fee may be applied to the use` IF `for the purposes of the Union or its constituent bodies`

GIVEN `constituted by regulations under the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted from that provision by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act provision applies to the body` IF
    `constituted by regulations under the Constitution` AND (NOT `exempted from that provision by Gazette order`)

§§ `4 -- execution under the common seal`

-- s 4(2): instruments requiring the seal "must be sealed with the common seal" and "must be signed by the Principal or a Deputy
-- Principal and by another member of the Board". (3): courts "take judicial notice of the common seal" and "presume that it was
-- duly affixed".
-- Constitution s 5(1): the Board is a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson, the Principal and 9 to 15 others. A Deputy Principal is not a
-- Board member by office; the Secretary is an officer, not a member (Constitution s 3(4)).
DECLARE Signatory IS ONE OF
    `the Principal`
    `a Deputy Principal`
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `an appointed Board member`
    `the Secretary of the Board`
    `a head of School`

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatory is a Board member by office` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Deputy Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an appointed Board member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatory is the Principal or a Deputy Principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Deputy Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatory is the Principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `sealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `first signatory` IS A Signatory, `second signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is executed as section 4 requires` IF
        `sealed`
    AND `the signatory is the Principal or a Deputy Principal` `first signatory`
    AND `the signatory is a Board member by office` `second signatory`
    AND (NOT (`the signatory is the Principal` `first signatory` AND `the signatory is the Principal` `second signatory`))

§§ `15 -- borrowing`

-- s 15: for its objects the Polytechnic "may raise loans from the Government or, with the approval of the Minister for Finance, raise
-- loans from banks or other financial institutions (whether in Singapore or elsewhere)" by mortgage, overdraft, charge, or debentures
-- or bonds.
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a bank or other financial institution`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender, `for the Polytechnic's objects` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister for Finance approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Polytechnic may raise the loan` IF
        `for the Polytechnic's objects`
    AND CONSIDER `the lender`
        WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a bank or other financial institution` THEN `the Minister for Finance approved`

§§ `Constitution ss 5, 7, 8 -- the Board's size, terms and vacancies`

-- s 5(1): the Board is "(a) a Chairperson; (b) a Deputy Chairperson; (c) the Principal; (d) such other persons, being not less than 9
-- and not more than 15, as may be determined by the Minister". (2): every member except the Principal is appointed by the Minister
-- and "unless the Minister otherwise directs, holds office for a period of 3 years" and is eligible for re-appointment.
-- s 7(1): the Minister may revoke a member's appointment, "except that of the Principal", if the member "becomes in the opinion of the
-- Minister unfit to continue in office or incapable of performing the member's duties"; (2) a member, except the Principal, may
-- resign "by giving written notice to the Minister".
-- s 8: a person appointed to a vacancy "must be appointed for the remainder of the term of the person's predecessor".
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board has a lawful number of members` IF
    `members` AT LEAST 12 AND `members` AT MOST 18

GIVEN `the Minister directed another term` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of an appointed member in years` MEANS
    IF `the Minister directed another term` THEN `directed term in years` ELSE 3

GIVEN `predecessor's term in years` IS A NUMBER, `years the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the replacement's term in years` MEANS
    `predecessor's term in years` MINUS `years the predecessor served`

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory, `the Minister thinks the member unfit or incapable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may revoke the appointment` IF
        `the signatory is a Board member by office` `the signatory`
    AND (NOT `the signatory is the Principal` `the signatory`)
    AND `the Minister thinks the member unfit or incapable`

§§ `Constitution ss 9, 2(5), 3(4) -- Board meetings and votes`

-- s 9(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Board is 6 members." (3): decisions by "a simple majority of the votes of the members
-- present and voting except that, in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or, in his or her absence, the Deputy
-- Chairperson has a casting vote". (5): if both are absent, a member elected by those present presides -- but s 9(3) gives that
-- member no casting vote. The encoding reads a tie with both absent as NOT carried (an INFERENCE: the text does not say).
-- s 2(5): the Principal may speak at any committee "but is not entitled to vote at the meeting unless the Principal is a member of
-- the committee". s 3(4): the Secretary may not vote on the Board unless "a member of the Board appointed to serve in that capacity".
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Deputy Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board motion is carried` IF
        `present` AT LEAST 6
    AND (   `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR (    `votes for` EQUALS `votes against`
             AND (`the Chairperson is present` OR `the Deputy Chairperson is present`)
             AND `the casting vote is for`))

GIVEN `a member of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Principal may vote at the committee meeting` IF `a member of the committee`

§§ `Constitution s 10 -- the Senate's quorum and meetings`

-- s 10(2): "The Senate must meet at least twice in each semester of every academic year". (3): "The quorum at every meeting of the
-- Senate is one quarter of the total number of members of the Senate."
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate meeting is quorate` IF
    `present` TIMES 4 AT LEAST `total members`

GIVEN `meetings in the semester` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate met often enough in the semester` IF
    `meetings in the semester` AT LEAST 2

§§ `Constitution s 14 -- the financial year`

-- s 14: "The financial year of the Polytechnic begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which the financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month number` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` MINUS 1

§§ `Constitution ss 17, 18 -- donations`

-- s 17(1): the Board may accept property and moneys "on any conditions that it may determine"; (2) records must be kept of all
-- donations "including the names of donors and any special conditions". s 18: property, moneys or funds "donated for any specific
-- purpose must be applied and administered in accordance with the purpose for which they may have been donated and must be
-- separately accounted for".
GIVEN `donated for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `the use is that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation may be applied to the use` IF
    (NOT `donated for a specific purpose`) OR `the use is that purpose`

GIVEN `donated for a specific purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation must be separately accounted for` IF `donated for a specific purpose`
